# THE GUEST ARCH SPLIT (aarch64 port, task A13). The reference build.ninja this file was
# generated from is x86-only and frozen, so the arm64 half is hand-written from darling PR
# 1753's src/libm/CMakeLists.txt: arm64 compiles a flat Source/ARM C list (FreeBSD msun
# transcendentals plus arm64_builtins.c hardware wrappers), with no .S, no SSE, the ARM
# include dir, -DARMLIBM_FENV_SUPPORT, and the arm_vfp alias in place of the Intel ones.
# system_m_extra is empty on arm64 (the xmm_* files are x86 SSE). Every _M_ARM branch below
# keys off this one flag; with it false the file is byte-identical to the generated original.
_M_ARM = host_info().arch.is_aarch64

# The flat arm64 source list, from PR 1753's TARGET_ARM64 libm_sources (Source/abs.c,
